/*****************************************************************************\
|*                      INetShell v3.25f Changes                             *|
\*****************************************************************************/

INSTALLATION:

o   In your INetShell/ directory, you will find a 2 files each of INet,
    INetConfig, and INetMaint.  Each with the follower of 3xx or 4xx.  These
    are the binaries for each version series of CNet Amiga.  Rename the
    proper versions of each executable to INet, INetConfig, INetMaint
    respectively.

    WARNING:  Use of the wrong binary for the version of CNet that you use could
    do almost anything, from guruing your system to corrupting your cnet data
    files.

o   Delete INetShell/help directory.  (if it still exists)

o   Perform a file by file check of the INetShell/Config directory.  Remove any
    non-custom (ie files that you have not added to the directory on your own).

o   If INetShell has been run since last system reset, and you are having the
    config files copied to RAM:  delete the INetShell directory from RAM:.

o   Make sure and update all of the INetShell/Text files.  Some of them may
    have changed.

    WARNING:  DO NOT MODIFY *ANY* OF THE FILES IN THE INETSHELL/TEXT DIRECTORY
    TO DO SO, CAN BE DANGEROUS TO YOUR SYSTEM.  YOU COULD GURU YOUR SYSTEM OR
    HAVE AS LITTLE DONE AS CAUSING YOUR SCREEN DISPLAYS BEING AFU.


REVISIONS   :

  3.25f (08/04/97)  - (IS) Was able to track down and fix the insufficient time
                           bug in INetShell.  (Thank you Tempest Bloodguad for
                           your help). Problem resulted from there not being
                           a bbscharges file in use or present.  INetShell now
                           will check for the existance of the file.
